save('resources/study-careers/coverage.html',wrap('Researcher Directory — Country Coverage',`<p>Where this directory has a useful institutional sample, and where it still needs work. This checklist includes continental Europe, existing programme destinations and additional regional priorities; it is not a list of every country in the world.</p><p class="notice">${researchers.length} distinct researchers are indexed across ${countryAudit.filter(c=>c.records).length} countries / territories. This is not a national faculty census or a ranking. Country refers to the indexed affiliation location, not citizenship. Counts do not establish supervision eligibility or current student places. A large single-school roster is still a single-institution sample.</p><p><a href="researchers.html">Researcher directory</a> · <a href="index.html">Study &amp; Careers</a> · <a href="../data/researcher-coverage.json">Download the count audit (JSON)</a></p><h2>This continental Europe batch</h2><p>${['France','Germany','Austria','Spain','Sweden','Netherlands','Belgium','Italy','Czech Republic'].map(n=>{const c=countryAudit.find(c=>c.country===n);return `<a href="#country-${n.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g,'-')}">${E(n)}: ${c.before} → ${c.records}</a>`}).join(' · ')}</p><h2>Country-by-country gaps</h2><p class="meta">Status describes the indexed sample only: 0 = not represented; 1–5 = very limited; larger samples are distinguished by whether one or several institution labels are present. No country is labelled complete. Filter Europe and “Not represented yet” to see remaining European gaps.</p>${controls(countryAudit,[['region','Region'],['status','Coverage status']])}${countryAudit.map(coverageEntry).join('\n')}${pagination()}`));
